  "Question": "The product of 5 nonzero rational numbers is positive. Which of the following could be the number of negative factors?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "4",
    "B": "1",
    "C": "3",
    "D": "5"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "For the product to be positive, the number of negative factors must be even. Among the choices, only 4 is even (there are 5 factors in total, and the remaining factor is positive).",
